WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.208 --> 00:00:02.002
- OK, Anthony Edwards.

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:02.794
First off,

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:04.004
thank you so much for joining

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:05.839
me on what is, like, one of the

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:08.216
biggest times of your life.

00:00:08.425 --> 00:00:10.385
When you wake up Wednesday morning,

00:00:10.427 --> 00:00:12.429
tell me the first thought that's

00:00:12.429 --> 00:00:13.555
gonna pop into your head.

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:17.142
- To be honest, probably gonna

00:00:17.142 --> 00:00:18.601
say I gotta feed and walk my dog.

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:20.603
- [Laughing]
- That's the,

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:22.022
that's the first thing I'm going to

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:22.856
say, but,

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:24.024
as far as, like, basketball-wise,

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:24.983
I'm just gon',

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:25.859
I'm probably gon' pray

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:26.026
and just,

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:27.277
whatever happens, happens.

00:00:27.569 --> 00:00:28.403
I'm not even gon' really

00:00:28.403 --> 00:00:29.738
think about where I'mma end up.

00:00:29.738 --> 00:00:31.239
Just whatever happens is supposed to happen.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.867
- You have said who wouldn't love

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:34.826
to be the No. 1 pick.

00:00:34.826 --> 00:00:36.828
So sell me. Tell me why you

00:00:36.828 --> 00:00:39.122
deserve to be the No. 1 pick.

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:42.792
- I feel like I deserve to be the No. 1 pick

00:00:42.792 --> 00:00:44.252
probably mostly because of

00:00:44.252 --> 00:00:45.462
the person I am off the court,

00:00:45.462 --> 00:00:46.755
not even on the court.

00:00:46.755 --> 00:00:47.589
Everybody—I feel like a lot of people

00:00:47.589 --> 00:00:48.840
know my abilities on the court.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:50.759
Just the person I am

00:00:50.759 --> 00:00:51.551
off the court, like,

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:52.635
just always smiling,

00:00:52.635 --> 00:00:54.137
I'm always happy and I'm

00:00:54.137 --> 00:00:55.138
never a negative person.

00:00:55.138 --> 00:00:56.306
So I just feel like that,

00:00:56.306 --> 00:00:57.307
that sums it all up.

00:00:58.349 --> 00:01:00.060
- You know, the top picks obviously are

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:03.063
expected to deliver results very quickly.

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:05.065
In what ways will you, and can

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:07.067
you, impact the game immediately?

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:10.195
- Just my playmaking ability,

00:01:10.195 --> 00:01:12.614
my ability to score the ball,

00:01:12.614 --> 00:01:15.075
my ability to score the ball from all three levels.

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:18.745
And I feel like my defensive potential.

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:19.162
- Yeah. I mean, I've watched

00:01:19.162 --> 00:01:20.580
a lot of interviews

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.748
that you've done recently, and you

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:24.334
always say, "Listen, defense is my thing.

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:25.335
I can play defense."

00:01:25.335 --> 00:01:26.961
Why is it so important to you to

00:01:26.961 --> 00:01:29.089
make sure, like, teams and fans know

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:30.840
that you can play some D?

00:01:31.508 --> 00:01:33.093
- I feel like, because like, it's a lot

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:35.345
of clips of college where I play defense,

00:01:35.345 --> 00:01:37.097
it's a lot of clips where I didn't play defense,

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:39.474
but I just want the world to know, like,

00:01:39.474 --> 00:01:40.642
that I really can defend the ball.

00:01:40.642 --> 00:01:42.060
Like, I can play really good defense. So.

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:44.229
- Yeah.
- I feel like we gon' see next year.

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:45.939
Like if I stay engaged and locked in

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:48.399
the whole time, the whole 72 games,

00:01:48.399 --> 00:01:50.819
people gon' see how good my defense really is.

00:01:50.985 --> 00:01:52.195
- Now I'm giving you a chance to

00:01:52.195 --> 00:01:53.530
deliver a message to the fanbase

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:55.532
of the team that drafts you.

00:01:55.532 --> 00:01:57.242
You know, you are now a part of

00:01:57.242 --> 00:01:59.244
this family, whatever team that is.

00:01:59.661 --> 00:02:00.662
What would you say to that

00:02:00.662 --> 00:02:01.746
fanbase?

00:02:02.747 --> 00:02:07.418
- Just ready to win a whole lot of games,
go to the playoffs, go to the conference finals

00:02:07.418 --> 00:02:08.503
and go to the Finals.

00:02:09.212 --> 00:02:10.380
- [Laughing]
- And I love, I love—

00:02:10.713 --> 00:02:12.006
I love to get in touch with the crowd.

00:02:12.006 --> 00:02:18.138
I mean, I love to, you know, pump the crowd up, 
talk to the crowd, so, y'all just be ready. Get it.

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:20.140
- Who are you most looking forward to

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.975
playing against when the season starts?

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:25.103
- Most definitely Kevin Durant.

00:02:25.103 --> 00:02:25.395
- Yeah.

00:02:25.395 --> 00:02:26.396
You love KD.

00:02:26.396 --> 00:02:27.689
You were talking about him when we,

00:02:27.689 --> 00:02:29.566
when we did that interview.

00:02:29.566 --> 00:02:31.526
You're also saying, like, that is somebody that

00:02:31.526 --> 00:02:33.528
you have had some communication with.

00:02:33.528 --> 00:02:36.990
Have you still?
- Yeah, yeah, he, yeah. Yeah, he—

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.283
- Yeah? Has he offered any good advice?

00:02:39.117 --> 00:02:41.244
- Nah, I wouldn't—nah.

00:02:42.036 --> 00:02:42.662
- Yeah. OK.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:46.291
Well, I do know—
- Cuz I, I gotta play against him, so—

00:02:46.291 --> 00:02:47.876
- Yeah, so, you're right, like, he's competition now!

00:02:47.876 --> 00:02:49.127
What's it gonna be like, though?

00:02:49.127 --> 00:02:50.420
When you step on the court, you'll

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:52.130
have to separate, you know, the fact

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:53.298
that he is one of your favorites.

00:02:54.257 --> 00:02:57.010
- Uh, I mean, when I enter the league,

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.678
it's not gonna be a favorite no more.

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:00.305
I'm gonna be my favorite.

00:03:00.305 --> 00:03:02.015
But when I wasn't in the league, I was, he was my

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:04.475
favorite. But once I—once Wednesday come,

00:03:04.475 --> 00:03:08.313
I don't have none of my favorites, 
so I'm not gonna feel no type of way.

00:03:08.313 --> 00:03:09.731
- Ooh, I love this. You're saying everything right.

00:03:10.565 --> 00:03:11.357
I know that you got to

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:12.775
speak with Michael Jordan,

00:03:12.775 --> 00:03:13.943
and you said that he gave

00:03:13.943 --> 00:03:15.069
you some tips on how to be

00:03:15.069 --> 00:03:17.071
more efficient in the mid post.

00:03:17.071 --> 00:03:18.448
What were some of those tips?

00:03:18.448 --> 00:03:19.490
I mean, you got basketball

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:20.366
tips from the GOAT.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:24.495
- Uh, man, it was just mostly

00:03:24.495 --> 00:03:27.165
like, just, you know, use your butt more

00:03:27.165 --> 00:03:28.791
in the post, in the mid post.

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:30.376
So I feel like that was

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:31.544
the best thing he told me.

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:32.837
And he was like, you are,

00:03:32.837 --> 00:03:34.172
and he was like, you stronger than I am.

00:03:35.173 --> 00:03:37.050
You more athletic. You bigger than me.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.801
And he was just like,

00:03:38.801 --> 00:03:40.970
use your butt more and create more space

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:42.055
and you gon' be unguardable.

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:44.098
So I just feel like hearing that

00:03:44.098 --> 00:03:46.768
was just, was just crazy because he

00:03:46.768 --> 00:03:48.228
actually came and watched me work out

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:49.938
and gave me some tools to take

00:03:49.938 --> 00:03:51.689
with me while I keep working out.

00:03:51.689 --> 00:03:53.650
So I feel like—

00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:56.361
- Yeah. I mean, for Michael Jordan to say,

00:03:56.361 --> 00:03:57.862
like, you're stronger than me already.

00:03:57.862 --> 00:03:58.821
I mean, how does that,

00:03:58.821 --> 00:03:59.864
how does that even feel,

00:03:59.864 --> 00:04:01.199
you know, to hear that and to

00:04:01.199 --> 00:04:03.284
know that he sees this potential?

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.079
- I can't even describe it, man.

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:08.122
It's just crazy, like, yeah, it

00:04:08.122 --> 00:04:09.958
was just crazy, him just being there.

00:04:10.708 --> 00:04:12.585
- You know, being a part of Klutch Sports

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:14.254
means you get to be around and learn

00:04:14.254 --> 00:04:17.006
from a bunch of NBA stars and leaders.

00:04:17.006 --> 00:04:17.882
So I wanna talk about

00:04:17.882 --> 00:04:18.841
a couple of those guys.

00:04:19.217 --> 00:04:20.843
Tell me, as specific as you can be:

00:04:21.135 --> 00:04:22.845
What have you learned from LeBron?

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:25.390
- Oh, I don't talk to those—

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:26.140
the only person that I

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:28.559
talked to all the time is Draymond Green.

00:04:28.559 --> 00:04:28.851
- OK, what have you

00:04:28.851 --> 00:04:30.019
learned from Draymond?

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:34.274
- He just, he just tell me, like,

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:35.108
just stay focused. Like, no matter what

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:36.901
happens, just stay focused.

00:04:36.901 --> 00:04:38.403
Just keep working.

00:04:38.403 --> 00:04:40.238
He tell me, he'd be like, you got it all,

00:04:40.238 --> 00:04:42.031
just keep working, stay grinding.

00:04:42.699 --> 00:04:43.866
Stay level-headed.

00:04:43.866 --> 00:04:45.159
Just keep workin', young fella,

00:04:45.159 --> 00:04:46.119
everything in front of you.

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:48.454
That's probably the only thing he tells me.

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:50.540
- All right, now, last time I spoke to you, 
it was actually

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:52.333
in the bubble when I was grabbing dinner

00:04:52.333 --> 00:04:54.460
with some friends, and Ja Morant was there,

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:56.337
and you guys were FaceTiming.

00:04:56.337 --> 00:04:58.256
I know you guys are super close.

00:04:58.256 --> 00:04:59.757
What advice has he given

00:04:59.757 --> 00:05:01.759
you during this predraft process?

00:05:03.052 --> 00:05:04.304
- Uh, kind of the same thing.

00:05:04.304 --> 00:05:05.763
He was just telling me, yeah,

00:05:05.763 --> 00:05:06.889
he was just telling me, like,

00:05:06.889 --> 00:05:08.599
it was, it's easy for him.

00:05:08.599 --> 00:05:09.642
Probably the most—he was

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:10.727
just like, it's easy for me,

00:05:10.727 --> 00:05:12.145
so it's not gon' be hard for you.

00:05:12.145 --> 00:05:13.771
He was like, you'd score

00:05:13.771 --> 00:05:15.064
the ball at a high clip,

00:05:15.064 --> 00:05:16.316
like I said, and he was just like,

00:05:16.316 --> 00:05:17.775
you can score the ball,

00:05:17.775 --> 00:05:18.651
so it's gon' be easy.

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:19.902
Like, you get switches with bigs.

00:05:19.902 --> 00:05:21.654
He was like, it's not, it's not as hard,

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:22.363
it's not as hard as

00:05:22.363 --> 00:05:23.990
people make it seem, so.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:26.451
- Yeah.
- I thought that was the best advice he gave me.

00:05:26.451 --> 00:05:26.909
- OK, nice.

00:05:26.909 --> 00:05:28.161
And last question for you.

00:05:28.619 --> 00:05:29.912
I know last time I talked

00:05:29.912 --> 00:05:31.497
to you, you love music.

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:34.459
So now what song from 2020

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.753
describes you and your game?

00:05:36.753 --> 00:05:37.587
You gotta pick one.

00:05:37.962 --> 00:05:40.506
- "Low Down" by Lil Baby.

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:41.758
- OK, why? Why "Low Down"?

00:05:41.758 --> 00:05:44.552
Good pick, but tell me why. [Laughing]

00:05:44.552 --> 00:05:47.221
- Just cuz, me and Lil Baby are from the same place.

00:05:47.221 --> 00:05:52.602
We both from Oakland City, 
and it's just, you know, we jell.

00:05:52.602 --> 00:05:53.644
We gon' be around each other.

00:05:53.644 --> 00:05:54.896
We just, you know what I'm sayin'?

00:05:54.896 --> 00:05:56.814
It's just, we cool.

00:05:56.814 --> 00:05:58.232
And I just, I love his music.

00:05:58.232 --> 00:05:58.649
So yeah.

00:05:58.649 --> 00:05:59.525
I feel like "Low Down"

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:00.360
is the best song for me.

00:06:00.777 --> 00:06:02.362
- Well, Anthony, it is amazing

00:06:02.362 --> 00:06:04.113
to talk to you as always.

00:06:04.113 --> 00:06:05.782
I'm looking forward to continuing

00:06:05.782 --> 00:06:07.533
to cover you through a very

00:06:07.533 --> 00:06:09.535
long and prosperous NBA career.

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:11.954
And most importantly, best

00:06:11.954 --> 00:06:13.498
of luck. I'll be watching.

00:06:13.498 --> 00:06:14.791
And I wish you the best.

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:16.209
- Thank you so much.

00:06:16.209 --> 00:06:20.421
Good talking to you.
- Good talking to you as always. Bye, Ant.
- Bye.

